-- A mixfix call whose first operand is itself a call. Before 2026-11-01 such a
-- call reached `l4 render` under its bare keyword, with no slots, so the rule
-- was read as an ordinary function: the operands went after the keyword and
-- the subject was lost, "is on or before the day x plus days 12 and the day y".
-- The same call with a plain name first read correctly. Now every mixfix call
-- is laid out by the pattern its definition declares.

DECLARE Day HAS n IS A NUMBER

GIVEN a IS A Day
      b IS A Day
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
a `is on or before` b MEANS a's n <= b's n

GIVEN a IS A Day
      b IS A Day
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
a `precedes` b MEANS a's n < b's n

GIVEN a IS A Day
      k IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Day
a `plus days` k MEANS Day (a's n + k)

GIVEN x IS A Day
      y IS A Day
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`in time` x y MEANS
       (x `is on or before` y)
   AND ((x `plus days` 12) `is on or before` y)
   AND (y `is on or before` (x `plus days` 12))
   AND ((y `plus days` 1) `is on or before` (x `plus days` 12))
   AND (`precedes` (x `plus days` 2) y)
